  "releaseNotes": "RoomSharp 0.4.2\n\n            - Significantly improved TypeConverter support with full, correct Nullable<T> materialization (including DateTime?, enums?, and numeric nullables).\n            - Fixed enum resolution issues by consistently using fully qualified type names across the source generator.\n            - Added clearer diagnostics for scenarios where database column types require TypeConverters.\n            - Introduced a zero-allocation, no-tracking query execution path for ultra-fast entity materialization.\n            - Major read performance improvements with drastically reduced GC pressure.\n            - Fully optimized TypeConverter pipeline with zero runtime allocations.\n            - Fixed multiple runtime mapping exceptions related to IL-generated conversions.\n            - Improved async query pipeline stability and ref-struct lifetime safety.\n            - Corrected Boolean handling across both SQLite and non-SQLite dialects.\n            - Prevented incorrect generation of no-tracking paths for DAOs that do not explicitly request it.\n            - Optimized generated code to reduce reflection usage and improve overall execution speed.\n            - Various reliability, safety, and code-generation correctness improvements throughout the DAO and mapper pipeline.\n            - Significant performance gains demonstrated in updated benchmarks compared to Dapper.",
